      {
        "id": 46444,
        "name": "TheSoundOfTrees",
        "username": "TheSoundOfTrees",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/da6949/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-25T01:02:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I only apply damage modifiers that depend on the target once I know for sure the final target of damage.</p><p>What I do is:</p><ol>\n<li>calculate damage done by Ambuscade, with only the modifiers that depend on him ( bonus to damage <em>dealt by</em> and so on) and so are always counted, whatever the target,</li>\n<li>determine the target of the attack and eventual redirections, based on the above damage value,</li>\n<li>only then apply modifiers that depend on the target ( damage taken modifers, damage <em>dealt to</em>, and so on).</li>\n</ol><p>However, this is how I do it (*), and the step by step process I chose because of this kind of problems, not an official ruling.</p><p>(*) : well, it is the simplified version of the step by step process I use, anyway.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:19:56.758Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
