        "username": "dypaca",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dypaca/{size}/2079_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-25T19:01:56.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"pppery\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/3d9bf3/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> pppery:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Then where does it say that modifiers are static?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I don't know of any official source that states it directly.&nbsp; It's just the general idea that if a card says \"Reduce damage dealt to Tempest by 1\", then it only reduces damage dealt to Tempest, and not damage that was aimed at Tempest but got redirected to Legacy.&nbsp; Depending on the specific cards, this can make more or less thematic sense, but it generally seems like the most reasonable way to play the game.</p>",
        "post_number": 8,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:19:56.993Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
